{
  "name": "Decide",
  "comment": "Decide which actions every step of this goal uses — the whole goal in two exchanges with the\ndecider, not one LLM call per step.\n\nThe decider is generic: it takes a state and typed questions and answers them. It knows nothing\nabout goals or steps. Everything goal-shaped is composed HERE: the state and the questions are\ntemplates (the words), and each step's Pick reads the answers (the numbers).\n\nStage 1 asks, per step, one choice — which module does the main work — and a yes/no per common\naction (decider.json). Stage 2 asks only what stage 1 left open, which each step's Pick decides:\nthe main module's action, a runner-up module, whether the step uses a module it scored under\ncertain, an if's branches, and on a step stage 1 was unsure of, which popular action it uses.\nStage 3 asks a follow-up only where stage 2 picked a coercion type that carries a kind a program\nnames (a number's decimal, an item's json, a generic's element); a build with none skips it.",
  "step": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "set %modules% = %!app.module.list%",
      "line": {
